From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 10:40:33 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(skills): drop orphaned deterministic negative fixtures
 (lint round-3)

Codex: the 'SonarCloud gate status for this PR' gates fixture I added in commit 1
was orphaned once round-2 switched PRECISION_CASES to a cleaner query, and that
exact wording routes to 'status' (the bare 'status' keyword out-scores sonarcloud).
The deterministic collision guards now live entirely in PRECISION_CASES (the test),
so evals.json should carry only positive + genuinely-semantic negatives. Removed
both deterministic negatives I had added (gates SonarCloud, worktree PR); reverted
those evals to their #430 state. The latent bare-'status' over-match (a W5-tier
disambiguation, not cleanly fixable deterministically without breaking /status) is
tracked in 5b1f4816.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
